Short:        Doom 3 for AmigaOS 3 on PiStorm (Pi 4, ogles2)
Author:       R-Typer, Ladislawv
Type:         game/shoot
Version:      @VERSION@
Architecture: m68k-amigaos >= 3.0
Requires:     PiStorm with Raspberry Pi 4, Emu68, RTG, Doom 3 1.3.1 data
Distribution: GPLv3 (game code); Doom 3's data not included

Doom 3 (id Software, 2004) running natively on a 68k Amiga with a PiStorm.
The game code runs on Emu68, the graphics are drawn by the Raspberry Pi 4's
VideoCore GPU through ogles2.library (OpenGL ES 2.0 for AmigaOS 3, included).
Based on dhewm3/d3es, the GPL release of Doom 3's source. Ported by R-Typer
and Ladislawv.

About 17 frames a second in Doom 3's own benchmark at 1920x1080 with the
Low settings; Medium and High settings, Paula or AHI sound, any RTG screen
size.

You need your own copy of Doom 3: the nine pak00?.pk4 files of version
1.3.1 (GOG.com, Steam, or a boxed copy with the 1.3.1 patch). The BFG
Edition does not work. The free 2004 demo's data works too.

Unpack, copy the game's pk4 files into Doom3/base/, double-click Doom3.
Everything else is in the ReadMe inside the archive.

Source code: @SOURCE@
